  "body": "`internal/gui/tests/codex-subagent-model.test.cjs` reads the Routing story after a fixed `page.waitForTimeout(300)` (line 192) instead of waiting for the clicked request's story. On a loaded machine (load ~380) it read the story of the request clicked before.\n\nSeen at 41737d214 (base 802fb6e61, change touches only Claude Code's subagent effort), `chromium en 1100px`, 29.9s:\n\n```\nCodex requested a subagent on gpt-5.5 and it stayed there: its subagents are set to token/gpt-6.1-sol, but its task was sealed by the ChatGPT backend that answered its lead, and only a ChatGPT account can open it.\nnot in\nCodex asked for gpt-5.5 → ChatGPTSubagent Codex requested a subagent on gpt-5.5; magpie put it on codex/gpt-6-astra, the model set for its subagents.me@example.com is the only account on for codex/gpt-6-astra — nothing to choose between.me@example.com (gpt-6-astra) answered in 900 ms · 1.2k tokens.\n```\n\nThe story shown is row 0's (\"moved\") while row 2's (\"sealed\") was expected. Run alone right after: 20/20 pass.\n\nFix: wait for the state, e.g. `await page.waitForFunction((s) => document.querySelector(\".rt-steps\")?.textContent.includes(s), said)` in place of the 300ms wait.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
