   "body": "I reproduced the stale-story failure and pushed a focused test fix: [435c03ac](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/435c03ac10c01e4f6b779fa40254cefd19bc5c10).\n\nThe test clicked a request, slept 300ms, then checked `.rt-steps`. If rendering took longer, it checked the previous request’s story. It now waits until the selected request’s expected story appears. The fixture delays the actual row handler by 600ms so this regression remains reproducible: the old 300ms version fails at both 1100px and 560px; the repaired version passes Chromium and WebKit, all five languages and both widths (20/20). No application assets or routing behavior changed. Playwright 1.62.1 ran in an isolated temporary container; its test directory, container and image have been removed.\n\nValidation on combined head [0437ae4c](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/0437ae4cf3be61c64546dc1573a8211e3c6ad7fd) (`fix/issue-batch-20261023-c`): Go 1.26.8, isolated HOME and pinned caches, umask 027; native/Linux-nogui/Windows vet and builds, full `go test -tags nogui ./... -count=1 -timeout=45m`, gofmt and diff checks. The preceding run exposed #3174; this combined branch includes its credited fixture fix. No production deployment or real subscription account was changed.\n",
